{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghhKbAUUvfauAsDwyZp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Answer: the high-spin to low-spin crossover happens at Dq ≈ 1958 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 19 580 cm⁻¹).** This is my estimate from diagonalising the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices for B = 922 cm⁻¹ and C = 4156 cm⁻¹, with no other approximations. I solved the eigenvalue problem by hand, so the last digit or two could be slightly off.\n\n**The two competing ground states**\n- High spin: ⁴T₁g, mainly the configuration t₂g⁵e_g².\n- Low spin: ²E_g, mainly the configuration t₂g⁶e_g¹.\n\n**⁴T₁g energy (2×2 matrix, B units except the Dq terms)**\nThe matrix mixes t₂⁵e² and t₂⁴e³:\n- Diagonal elements: −12B − 8Dq and −3B + 2Dq.\n- Off-diagonal element: 6B.\n\nThe lower root is:\nE(⁴T₁) = −7.5B − 3Dq − √[(4.5B + 5Dq)² + 36B²]\n\n**²E_g energy (4×4 matrix)**\nI used the d³ ²E matrix with the sign of Dq reversed, which is the hole equivalence for d⁷. Basis order: t₂³, t₂²(¹A₁)e, t₂²(¹E)e, e³.\n- Diagonal elements:\n  - −6B + 3C + 12Dq\n  - 8B + 6C + 2Dq\n  - −B + 3C + 2Dq\n  - −8B + 4C − 18Dq\n- Off-diagonal elements:\n  - −6√2·B (t₂³ with t₂²(¹A₁)e)\n  - −3√2·B (t₂³ with t₂²(¹E)e)\n  - 10B (between the two t₂²e states)\n  - √3(2B + C) (t₂²(¹A₁)e with e³)\n  - 2√3·B (t₂²(¹E)e with e³)\n\nTwo checks confirm the matrix: its trace equals the sum of the free-ion ²G, ²H and two ²D energies, and the ⁴T₁ roots reduce to ⁴F and ⁴P at Dq = 0.\n\n**Numerical results**\n\n| Dq (cm⁻¹) | E(⁴T₁) (cm⁻¹) | E(²E) (cm⁻¹) | Ground state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1800 | −26 580 | −25 030 | high spin (⁴T₁) |\n| 1960 | −27 801 | −27 820 | low spin (²E) |\n\nNear the crossing, ²E falls about 9.8 cm⁻¹ per cm⁻¹ of Dq faster than ⁴T₁. Interpolating from the Dq = 1960 point gives a crossing at Dq ≈ 1958 cm⁻¹.\n\nFor comparison, using only the diagonal (pure-configuration) energies, without configuration interaction, would put the crossing near 10Dq ≈ 4C − 5B ≈ 20 000 cm⁻¹, slightly higher.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1958, \"B\": 922, \"C\": 4156, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Crossing of 4T1g and 2Eg found by full Tanabe-Sugano matrix diagonalization at Dq ≈ 1958 cm^-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fbfe3e5-789a-4a27-8c6f-cf9327d1d85c","uuid":"04c6a928-ce9a-4fea-b206-36f0e3289a1c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:03:33.407Z","request_id":"req_011CghhKaiCCX23NAefcTPy2"}
